#######
# Setup
#######

$initial = 70;
$rate = random(10,15);
$final = random(35,45);
Context("LinearRelation")->variables->are(t => 'Real');
$equation = LinearRelation("$initial - $rate t = $final");

#############################
# Exercise Group Introduction
#############################

BEGIN_PGML
Write an equation to model the scenario. There is no need to solve the equation.

END_PGML

######
# Body
######

BEGIN_PGML
On a cold snowy day, the temperature in your home is a cozy [`[$initial]\,^{\circ}F\text{,}`] but then you lose power and heating. Your home temperature begins to drop at a rate of [`[$rate]\,\frac{^{\circ}F}{\text{hour}}\text{.}`] How long will it take before your home is [`[$final]\,^{\circ}F\text{?}`] Write an equation to model this scenario. There is no need to solve it.

[@KeyboardInstructions('Use [|t|]* as the variable.')@]**

[_]{$equation}{20}

END_PGML

#############
# End Problem
